{"body":{"text":["A statement has no name and no address of its own, as quotes had by their numbers: \"naturally, the statement doesn't have such an address\" (23/116); it is reached by its id, as the session drew it (23/115). It points at its ground, the utterances or sentences it rests on, the author's words or the session's (23/80), which components might show by their numbers (23/116)."]},"id":"1M89M74W6GR5000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Every statement has a **status**, where it stands now: open, asked and not decided; proposed, the session's and not taken up; leaning, the author's, inclined to with doubt; settled, decided by the author; closed, no longer holding. These are Knowledge's own marks, with closed beside them, as the session drew them (23/91, 23/119, 23/135, 23/137). Each status points at what gave it, the utterance of the decision, and so whose it was, as the session drew it (23/129). A statement's history is its versions (23/132)."]},"id":"1M89M74W6GR5001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}